Package: gridy
Type: Package
Title: Protect Multilevel Gridded Data with a Quadtree Approach
Version: 0.1.2
Description: Builds variable-resolution grids from geolocated data in order to
  disseminate them under a frequency threshold rule. Several nested square
  grids are overlaid, from the coarsest to the finest, and each cell is walked
  down the resulting quadtree, a cell whose count reaches the threshold is
  disseminated on its own, while cells below it are merged with their
  neighbours until the threshold is met. Cell identifiers follow the Inspire
  specification for statistical units. Helpers are provided to extract the
  resulting natural grid, to estimate sensitive variables over protected cells
  by proportional allocation, and to convert cell identifiers into 'sf'
  polygons.
